{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013020-mixed-gameline-questions-again","id":1013020,"title":"Mixed gameline questions (again)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-05T22:54:06-08:00","id":1013020,"title":"Mixed gameline questions (again)","content":"I'm going to be running a campaign combining 5 or 6 gamelines (Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling, Hunter, Geist, &amp; perhaps Mage). The players will be 1 of each sort working together in a group.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if having a custom merit that would allow the group to function mechanically as each character's 'class social group' (i.e. coterie, pack, motley, cell, etc.) would work. Could that be overpowered, or am I overthinking things? Granted, the tension between their own 'native' group &amp; this odd assortment could be interesting, but coming up w/ 6 different NPC-populated groups would be a ton of work.<br /> <br /> So... who else has done mixed gameline campaigns? How did you handle this particular aspect of it? What other aspects proved challenging, or rewarding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T00:52:08-08:00","id":1013058,"title":"","content":"All the gamelines have different core themes that speak to a particular aspect of the human experience, and to various Traditional Monster Stories and Horror Tropes. Trying to meld them together in the narrative is going to be mind-boggling; everyone has different agendas and urges they pursue! Having overpowered Merit is likely to be a lesser concern, compared to that.<br /> <br /> Like, take vampires and werewolves for instance. They could probably agree on how they have an urge to hunt, and what it feels like to have an inner Dark Self. But the vampire must cling on to what's left of his Humanity to remain sane, while the werewolf sometimes has to act completely inhuman to stay Harmonious. And with both of them being generally harmful to humans, hunters are not going to be happy with them. And all the magical ruckus they cause might draw some unwanted attention, which a changeling would try to avoid just in case the attention is Strange in nature. Oh, but the mage wants the magical shenanigans to spread, because for him Arcane knowledge is Supernal power. And all in the background, the Bound complains why everyone isn't helping him exorcise and/or counsel ghosts... or just says &quot;Ah, whatever&quot; and decides to tag along the fun ride.<br /> <br /> Say, has anyone in your group considered playing a Beast? The template and the gameline come with ways for holding a better crossover campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T01:29:04-08:00","id":1013064,"title":"","content":"I believe the best approach would be to have one of the players choose to be the &quot;leader&quot; of the group and then just play the social group as if it were that gameline. (I.E. It would be a Pack if the Uratha called the shots, Coterie if the Kindred was the boss, Ect.)<br /> <br /> That way you wouldn't need to bother with making a custom merit, plus the social dynamics of the group would then have an outline for the Troupe to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T02:14:17-08:00","id":1013073,"title":"","content":"A Pack is already allowed to have weird things in it, so that's probably your best bet here. Plus, totem benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T09:31:43-08:00","id":1013220,"title":"","content":"Here's where I'm seeing uniting themes:<br /> <br /> - Protect our Realm (whether you call it the Flesh Realm, the Fallen Realm, whatever) from incursion(s) by Things From Beyond. This should get on board Werewolves, Changelings, Hunters, Ghostwalkers (I abhor the term 'sin-eaters; hope 2e changes that), &amp; possibly Mages (at least if the Beyond is the Abyssal; &amp; at least willing to go along for knowledge otherwise). Could even possibly work in a vampire w/ a view to 'sustainable farming' who doesn't want the kine all slaughtered or dragged off to wherever leaving the Kindred to starve.<br /> <br /> - Keep humanity from learning the truth. This should get on board vampires for certain. Maybe some of the others depending on their individual outlook.<br /> <br /> As for the differing styles of dealing w/ problems, I see that as magnificent grist for the dramatic interplay of the chronicle. What do the characters who prefer a subtle approach do when Fido wolfs out &amp; slaughters something - never mind that she got the job done &amp; prevented a greater loss of life which their approach would have permitted? What does the mage do when everyone else just wants to kill the 'Wyrd Thynge' rather than studying it - never mind how it was warping reality &amp; probably would've brought all kinds of greater threats their way? When someone comes up w/ a plan to defeat the BBEG that requires traveling deep into the Hedge, is the changeling going to be able to hold it together and execute the plan or is he going to crack &amp; flee - leaving the others stranded? Becoming a functional team despite their differences - even turning those differences into strengths - can be a great dynamic to explore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013020-mixed-gameline-questions-again?p=1013064#post1013064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the best approach would be to have one of the players choose to be the &quot;leader&quot; of the group and then just play the social group as if it were that gameline. (I.E. It would be a Pack if the Uratha called the shots, Coterie if the Kindred was the boss, Ect.)<br /> <br /> That way you wouldn't need to bother with making a custom merit, plus the social dynamics of the group would then have an outline for the Troupe to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the idea of having it function under the dynamics of a single gameline group, &amp; it is largely modeled after a Hunter cell (of a larger &amp; ancient conspiracy). If I do that, however, do the ENEs wind up getting conspiracy benefits? They're already going to be stronger than the Hunter; giving endowments to the hunter exclusively was going to be a big part of letting him narrow that gap a bit.<br /> <br /> OTOH, if I go for something else, like a werewolf pack, would everyone then gain access to something there, even the non-Uratha members of the pack? I've only just started in on the WtF rules, so I'm unclear on how that works for them. This could be a great boon to the hunter, but would it potentially boost some others too much?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T09:40:20-08:00","id":1013226,"title":"","content":"Everyone in a pack gets totem benefits. Even the humans who might not even know they're in a pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:55:21-08:00","id":1013339,"title":"","content":"There is, at first, no need for a Merit for what you want. Most effects meant for a group won't be affected by the group being mixed. A pack don't have to be made of werewolves, a coterie don't need to be all-vampire, and so on. Changelings can devise the group's Oath in a way that the non-fae members are affected all the same. As soon as the characters consider their companions as members of the group, it doesn't matter if such companions are of the same kind or not.<br /> <br /> A few effects won't work because they are based on the splat's specific characteristics. You can't affect how a vampire uses Auspice's Gifts, because a vampire doesn't have either Gifts, nor an Auspice. Then it is at your discretion to develop a way around it. But simply making a single Merit for &quot;being considered the other&quot; won't work, it is a far more complex and specific, case-by-case, conundrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}